          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            %em Exact real computer arithmetic
            refers to treatment of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+number"} real number
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arithmetic"} arithmetic
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/computation"} computers
            to finite (necessarily) but arbitrary precision. This is in contrast with what is called
            %span.newWikiWord
              floating-point arithmetic
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/floating-point+arithmetic"} ?
            which uses just one fixed finite approximation of the real numbers by
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers"} natural numbers
          %p
            Exact real computer arithmetic essentially implements what in mathematical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/computability+theory"} computability theory
            is known as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Type+Two+Theory+of+Effectivity"} type-II theory
            (in contrast to the “type-I” theory of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+recursive+functions"} partial recursive functions
            acting just on
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers"} natural numbers
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/computable+function+%28analysis%29"} computable function (analysis)
            is the core topic of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+analysis"} constructive analysis
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+analysis"} exact analysis
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+domain+theory"} topological domain theory
          %h2#references References
          %p
            For more see the references at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+number"} real number
            and at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
